{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"ee1108aa-931d-491b-bf17-b3a98f3c535a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Target Files\n- `schema.py`\n- `upcaster.py`\n- `store.py`\n- `projector.py`\n\n### Symbols \u0026 Line Ranges\n- `schema.py`: `Event.__post_init__` (lines 16–20)\n- `upcaster.py`: `upcast` (lines 7–20)\n- `store.py`: `EventStore.append` (lines 15–27), `EventStore.read` (lines 29–32)\n- `projector.py`: `replay` (lines 15–21)\n\n### Invariants \u0026 Exact Changes\n- **`schema.py` (`Event.__post_init__`)**:\n  - Validate `schema_version`: must be `type(self.schema_version) is int` and `self.schema_version in (1, 2, 3)` (rejects `bool` and other ints/types with `ValueError`).\n  - Keep existing checks: `event_type == \"increment\"`, `isinstance(payload, dict)`, `type(stream_version) is int and stream_version \u003e= 0`.\n- **`upcaster.py` (`upcast`)**:\n  - Fix chaining: replace `if result.schema_version == 1: ... elif result.schema_version == 2: ...` with sequential `if result.schema_version == 1:` followed by `if result.schema_version == 2:` so v1 chains through v2 to v3.\n  - Handle missing `\"amount\"` in v1 payload: `payload.pop(\"amount\")` would raise `KeyError`; instead check `\"amount\" in payload` (or raise `ValueError` if missing).\n  - Validate `result.schema_version == 3`, `type(delta) is int` (rejects `bool`), and `isinstance(result.payload.get(\"metadata\"), dict)` before returning `Event(...)`.\n- **`store.py` (`EventStore.append`)**:\n  - Fix `expected_version` check: `if type(expected_version) is not int or expected_version != current:` (currently `expected_version \u003e current`, which fails to reject `expected_version \u003c current`).\n  - Deep-copy each event in `batch` before validating/mutating `stream_version`, so caller `Event` objects are never mutated.\n  - Validate every item in `batch` (`isinstance(event, Event)` and `event.__post_init__()`) before mutating `self._streams`.\n  - Return `deepcopy(stored_batch)` (independent copies of appended `Event`s) so mutating the returned list/events does not affect stored events.\n- **`store.py` (`EventStore.read`)**:\n  - Return `[deepcopy(e) for e in self._streams.get(stream_id, [])[after_version:]]` (or filter by `e.stream_version \u003e after_version` with `deepcopy`) so callers cannot mutate stored events or nested payloads.\n- **`projector.py` (`replay`)**:\n  - Pass `after_version=version` (instead of `after_version=0`) to `store.read(stream_id, after_version=version)` so snapshot replay only replays the tail after the snapshot version.\n\n### Verify Command\n- `pytest -q --tb=short`\n","duration_seconds":8.0595009,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":28324,"output_tokens":1125,"thinking_tokens":72,"cache_read_tokens":22306,"total_tokens":29449}}}
